# Layout Law

**Principle:** Content must never bleed off-screen. Use flex for deterministic centering.

## Centering

- **Stacked content:** `display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; width: 100%`
- **Avoid:** `text-align: center` alone for buttons (subpixel drift on iOS)
- **Block elements with max-width:** Add `margin-inline: auto` to center

## No Bleed

- Content must never touch viewport edges.
- Test at 320px — verify visible space on left and right.
- **Page-level:** `overflow-x: hidden; max-width: 100vw` on html/body.
- **Never:** `width: 100vw` (causes scrollbar issues).

## Responsive Breakpoints

Test at: **320px, 375px, 768px, 1024px, 1280px**

Mobile-first: base styles = 320px minimum; scale up with `clamp()` or media queries.

## Quick Reference — Common Patterns

```css
/* Container */
.container {
  width: 100%;
  max-width: 1200px;
  margin-inline: auto;
  padding-inline: clamp(1rem, 4vw, 1.5rem);
}

/* Centered section */
.section {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
  width: 100%;
}

/* CTA button */
.cta-btn {
  padding: clamp(0.75rem, 2vw, 1rem) clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
  min-height: 44px;
}
```

## Anti-Patterns

- `text-align: center` alone for centering stacked buttons
- `width: 100vw`

